--- !u!114 &10395
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 3148}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name:
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "“Don’t even get me started on how hard it was to get permission to carry this thing. The amount of paperwork was absurd. I had to get at least three written letters from my colleagues that said I was of “good character”. Like I was planning a shooting in a facility with armed guards around every corner. Then I had to go through some “Breach Response Training Course” to prove I knew how to use the thing.\r\n\r\nEven after I got approval to bring it into the facility, and registered it with the workstation database, they still won’t let me carry it concealed. It always has to be kept in a clearly-visible holster. At this point, I’m just parading the thing around for all the D-Class to see. If one of them ends up grabbing it and holding me hostage, or just flat-out killing me, I wouldn’t be surprised.\r\n\r\nThe idea of me needing to defend myself is such a wild concept to whoever runs this place, that I’m starting to wonder if going through the approval process was even worth it. \r\n\r\nI’m telling you now, if they don’t give me permission to carry it concealed soon, it is bound to get misused.”\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b40e27b94d22bbf4d8ed598c1c3f329b, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2100000, guid: 03c51d5289a83a84f80bbf2ab954cca7, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
  m_fontMaterials: []
